statement:
给定一个长度为 n 的链表，每个节点除 next 外还有一个 random 指针，可以指向链表中任意节点或为空。请构造这条链表的深拷贝：新链表由 n 个全新节点组成，值与原节点一一对应，且新节点的 next 和 random 只指向新链表中的节点，使新链表与原链表结构完全相同。返回新链表的头节点；原链表在返回时必须保持不变。

数据用二维数组表示：第 i 行为 [val, randomIndex]，randomIndex 为 random 指向的节点下标（从 0 开始），空指针为 -1。评测以同样的格式输出你返回的链表；若返回的链表含有原链表的节点、random 指向新链表之外，或原链表被修改，判为错误。

节点定义（已提供）：class Node { public: int val; Node* next; Node* random; Node(int _val); };

en.statement:
You are given a linked list of length n in which each node has, besides next, a random pointer that may point to any node in the list or be null. Construct a deep copy of the list: the new list consists of n brand-new nodes whose values correspond one-to-one with the original nodes, and the new nodes' next and random pointers point only to nodes of the new list, so that the new list has exactly the same structure as the original. Return the head of the new list; the original list must be unchanged when you return.

Data is represented as a 2D array: row i is [val, randomIndex], where randomIndex is the 0-based index of the node random points to, or -1 for null. The judge prints your returned list in the same format; it is judged wrong if the returned list contains original nodes, a random pointer points outside the new list, or the original list was modified.

Node definition (provided): class Node { public: int val; Node* next; Node* random; Node(int _val); };

